auditcore_llm_client 0.1.0 — attribution and authorization

New implementation in auditcore. The behaviour was taken from the executed
ai-router clients of janpow77/audit_designer (commit
ccd65245182982af3ef885a7a6d43583f4f72cbb, backend/app/utils/ai_router_client.py),
janpow77/flowinvoice (commit fb2d18568d2eaf64574d131ceae51a936b9aac02,
backend/app/clients/ai_router_client.py, backend/app/llm/ollama.py),
janpow77/audit-portal (commit d8eefa426826bdecb67036774f3128ae05e7d0d0,
backend/app/clients/ai_router_client.py) and janpow77/cockpit (commit
df203d4c33e786eb8a8ad3fe53b3b7eb9241d406, src/cockpit/services/ai_router_client.py).
Routes and request/response contracts were read from janpow77/ai-router (commit
426cd78e86df9f822452af035b8d58a19f7aa820) and janpow77/flow-agent (commit
149e14be8952fddacb7601753dd2bf133fca51cb). Timeouts, health thresholds, route
fallbacks, field mappings and redaction patterns were adopted; the code was
rewritten. Blob SHAs of every source file are listed in provenance.json.

On 2026-09-22 the rights holder decided: "die Bibliotheken sollen MIT sein,
die anderen Repos nicht; die Bibliotheken kommen nach auditcore". On
2026-09-25 the rights holder asked to build this library from the app clients.
Status: USER_AUTHORIZED_MIT for this library only; the source repositories
keep their own licensing.

No third-party code is included. The optional extra "http" uses httpx
(BSD-3-Clause) as an ordinary dependency.
